WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.512
GroupBy is one of the most important patterns in Pandas.

00:00:03.512 --> 00:00:07.702
A useful way to understand it is split, apply, combine.

00:00:07.702 --> 00:00:13.637
First, Pandas splits the rows into groups based on a category.

00:00:13.637 --> 00:00:16.812
Then it applies a calculation within each group.

00:00:16.812 --> 00:00:20.587
Finally, it combines the results into a summary.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:25.207
In this example, we groupby channel and sum the amount column.

00:00:25.207 --> 00:00:29.432
Click Run. The result tells us total revenue for web, email, and store.

00:00:29.432 --> 00:00:35.812
Now connect that code to a business question: which channel contributes the most revenue?

00:00:35.812 --> 00:00:37.177
That is the important part.

00:00:37.177 --> 00:00:45.542
GroupBy is not just syntax; it is a way to answer questions at a different level of detail.

00:00:45.542 --> 00:00:48.772
The original table has one row per order.

00:00:48.772 --> 00:00:52.527
The grouped result has one row or value per channel.

00:00:52.527 --> 00:00:57.187
Whenever you group data, ask what one output row represents.

00:00:57.187 --> 00:01:01.489
This is the same concept of grain that we discussed during duplicate handling.
